# Module overview

| Module | Flag | Default | Linux | Windows | macOS | Android | iOS |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Tray | `tray` | on | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | — | — |
| Updater | `updater` | on | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | — (stores) | — (App Store) |
| Media server | `media_server` | on | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | — | — |
| SQL | `sql` | on | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| File watching | `fs_watch` | on | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | — |
| Dialogs | `dialog` | on | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ (SAF) | ✓ (document picker) |
| Notifications | `notification` | on | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| Settings store | `store` | on | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| App menu | `menu` | on | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | — | — |
| Global shortcuts | `global_shortcut` | on | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | in-app (Meta+/ list) | — |
| Input injection | `input` | on | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | — (the Oriel keyboard) | — |
| Clipboard | `clipboard` | on | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| Deep links | `deep_link` | **off** | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| Vector search | `sqlite_vec` | **off** | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| LLM inference | `llama` | **off** | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| Speech-to-text | `whisper` | **off** | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| Audio capture | `audio_capture` | **off** | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ (AAudio) | ✓ |
| Dictation | `whisper` + `audio_capture` | **off** | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ (+ system recognizer) | ✓ |
| Chat (LLM) | `llama` | **off** | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |

On Android and iOS, a module marked — is off by default and a build error when turned on: the platform has no such thing (a tray, system-wide hotkeys) or forbids it. [Android and iOS]($link.page('docs/mobile')) has what replaces them.

All modules build for Linux, Windows and macOS. Native dependencies (`sqlite_vec`, `llama`, `whisper`, `audio_capture`) are **off by default** and opt-in via `-D` flags. To disable a default-on module, pass `-D<name>=false`.

# Tray icon

System tray icon with a clickable menu. Left-click toggles the app window visibility.

```zig
tray = try oriel.tray.Tray.create(gpa, .{
    .id = "com.example.App",
    .title = "My App",
    .icon = .{ .png = @embedFile("icon.png") },
    .menu = &.{
        .{ .item = .{ .id = "show", .label = "Show" } },
        .{ .check = .{ .id = "dnd", .label = "Do not disturb" } },
        .{ .separator = {} },
        .{ .item = .{ .id = "quit", .label = "Quit" } },
    },
    .on_menu = onTrayMenu,
});
```

**Platform support:** Linux (StatusNotifierItem + DBusMenu) · Windows (Shell_NotifyIconW) · macOS (`NSStatusItem`; right-click opens the menu).

# Updater

Built-in self-updater with Ed25519 signature verification and atomic binary replacement. Emits progress events and restarts the app.

```zig
const Updater = oriel.updater.Commands(.{
    .app_id = "com.example.App",
    .manifest_url = "https://releases.example.com/latest.json",
    .current_version = "1.0.0",
    .public_key_b64 = app.update_public_key orelse @panic("missing key"),
});

pub const Commands = struct {
    pub const updater_check = Updater.updater_check;
    pub const updater_install = Updater.updater_install;
    pub const async_commands = .{ "updater_check", "updater_install" };
};
```

See [Code signing]($link.page('docs/signing')) for key generation and signing updates.

**Platform support:** Linux · Windows (tested under Wine) · macOS (plain executables, and whole `.app` bundles with the `app.tar.gz` format, swapped atomically).

# Media server

HTTP server streaming large video and audio files with range-request support (RFC 9110). No need to load multi-GB files into memory.

```zig
var media: oriel.media_server.Server = undefined;
try media.start(io, gpa, .{
    .root_dir = "/home/me/Videos",
    .port = 17893,
    .allowed_origin = "app://app",
});
defer media.stop();
```

Also available at `app://app/media/<path>` for fetch requests (WebKitGTK's media player requires http(s), so use the TCP server for `<video>` tags).

**Platform support:** Linux · Windows (tested under Wine) · macOS (`app://app/media/` streamed through `WKURLSchemeHandler`).

# SQL and SQLite

Embedded SQLite database with optional vector search (`sqlite_vec`). Thread-safe, persistent storage.

```zig
const db = try oriel.sql.Db.open("data.db");
defer db.close();

const stmt = try db.prepare("CREATE TABLE items (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT);");
defer stmt.finalize();
_ = try stmt.step();
```

**Platform support:** Linux · Windows · macOS.

## Vector search (`-Dsqlite_vec`)

Adds the `sqlite-vec` extension for k-nearest-neighbor (KNN) vector search:

```zig
try db.exec("CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE embeddings USING vec0(data float[384]);");

var insert = try db.prepare("INSERT INTO embeddings (rowid, data) VALUES (?, ?);");
defer insert.finalize();
try insert.bindBlob(1, oriel.sqlite_vec.asBytes(&vector));
_ = try insert.step();
```

**Status:** Opt-in with `-Dsqlite_vec` (requires `-Dsql`). Default: off.

# File watching

Monitor directories for file changes and receive events:

```zig
try oriel.fs_watch.watch(gpa, "/home/me/Documents", onFileChange);
```

**Platform support:** Linux (inotify) · Windows (`ReadDirectoryChangesW`) · macOS (FSEvents).

# Dialogs

Native file open/save dialogs:

```zig
const file = try oriel.dialog.openFile(gpa, .{
    .title = "Select a file",
    .filters = &.{ .{ .name = "Text", .patterns = &.{ "*.txt" } } },
});
```

**Platform support:** Linux (`GtkFileDialog`) · Windows (`IFileOpenDialog`) · macOS (`NSOpenPanel` / `NSSavePanel`).

# Notifications

System desktop notifications:

```zig
try oriel.notification.notify(.{
    .title = "Processing complete",
    .body = "Your export is ready.",
});
```

**Platform support:** Linux (`GNotification`) · Windows (balloon tooltips) · macOS (`UNUserNotificationCenter` in an `.app`; `osascript` fallback when unbundled).

# Settings store

Thread-safe JSON key-value store with atomic writes. Standard directories per OS (XDG on Linux, Known Folders on Windows, `~/Library/Application Support` and `~/Library/Caches` on macOS):

```zig
var store = try oriel.store.Store.open(gpa, "dev.example.App", "settings");
defer store.deinit();
try store.set("theme", "dark");
try store.save();

const theme = store.getString("theme");
```

Also provides `configDir`, `dataDir`, `cacheDir` helpers.

**Platform support:** Linux · Windows · macOS.

# App menu bar

Native application menu bar:

```zig
try oriel.App.setMenu(&.{
    .{ .submenu = .{ .label = "File", .items = &.{
        .{ .item = .{ .id = "new", .label = "New", .shortcut = "<Control>n" } },
        .{ .separator = {} },
        .{ .item = .{ .id = "quit", .label = "Quit", .shortcut = "<Control>q" } },
    } } },
}, onMenuAction);
```

**Platform support:** Linux (`GMenuModel`) · Windows (Win32 menus; tested under Wine) · macOS (`NSMenu`, between the default App and Edit/Window menus; `<Ctrl>` becomes ⌘).

# Global shortcuts

Register system-wide keyboard shortcuts that trigger even when the app is unfocused:

```zig
try oriel.global_shortcut.register(gpa, .{
    .id = "rewrite_hotkey",
    .description = "Rewrite selected text",
    .trigger = "CTRL+ALT+G",
}, &onHotkey);
```

**Platform support:** Linux (Wayland GlobalShortcuts portal + X11 XGrabKey) · Windows (`RegisterHotKey`; tested under Wine) · macOS (Carbon `RegisterEventHotKey`, no permission needed).

# Input injection

Simulate keyboard input and clipboard operations:

```zig
try oriel.input.typeText("Hello from Zig!");
try oriel.input.keyCombo("ctrl+v");
```

**Platform support:** Linux (Wayland virtual-keyboard + X11 XTest) · Windows (`SendInput`; tested under Wine) · macOS (`CGEvent`; needs the Accessibility permission, else `error.AccessibilityNotGranted`).

# Clipboard

Background clipboard read/write for text and PNG images:

```zig
const text = try oriel.clipboard.readText(gpa);
try oriel.clipboard.writeText("New content");
```

**Platform support:** Linux (Wayland data-control + X11 GdkClipboard) · Windows · macOS (`NSPasteboard`).

# Deep links

Handle custom URL schemes (e.g. `myapp://note/123`), delivering links to both cold-starting and already-running app instances.

```zig
if (oriel.options.deep_link) {
    oriel.deep_link.onOpen(onDeepLink);
}

fn onDeepLink(url: []const u8) void {
    // Validated against declared schemes, max 2048 bytes, no control chars
    std.log.info("Received deep link: {s}", .{url});
}
```

In the webview frontend:

```ts
import { listen } from "./oriel";

// Listen for incoming deep links
listen("deep-link", ({ url }) => {
    console.log("Deep link received:", url);
});

// Or query the cold-start URL
const initialUrl = await window.oriel.deepLink.current();
```

Configure schemes in `build.zig` via `.package = .{ .url_schemes = &.{"myapp"} }` or using the CLI:

```sh
oriel deep-link add myapp
```

**Platform support:** Linux (GApplication single-instance + XDG desktop handler) · Windows (Named mutex + `WM_COPYDATA` forwarding + HKCU registry) · macOS (Info.plist `CFBundleURLTypes` in the `.app`; Launch Services delivers links as `kAEGetURL` Apple Events, to the running instance if there is one; `oriel deep-link register` runs `lsregister` on `zig-out/<Name>.app`).

**Status:** Opt-in with `-Ddeep_link`. Default: off.

# Local AI inference

## LLM text generation (`-Dllama`)

Embedded llama.cpp for local text generation. Use quantized models (GGUF format):

```zig
oriel.llama.initBackend();
defer oriel.llama.deinitBackend();

const model = try oriel.llama.loadModel("path/to/model.gguf", params);
defer model.deinit();
```

Build time: ~45 seconds cold; cached builds are fast. CPU features auto-detected; for distribution, use `-Dcpu=x86_64_v2` or `-Dcpu=baseline`.

**Status:** Opt-in with `-Dllama`. Default: off.

**GPU:** CUDA on Linux with `-Dggml_cuda`; Metal on macOS (on by default).

## Speech recognition (`-Dwhisper`)

Embedded whisper.cpp for speech-to-text:

```zig
oriel.whisper.initBackend();
defer oriel.whisper.deinitBackend();

const ctx = try oriel.whisper.loadModel("path/to/ggml-model.bin", params);
defer ctx.deinit();
```

Same build-time and distribution considerations as llama.

**Status:** Opt-in with `-Dwhisper`. Default: off.

**GPU:** CUDA on Linux with `-Dggml_cuda`; Vulkan on Linux, Windows and Android with `-Dggml_vulkan`; Metal on macOS and iOS (on by default).

For live dictation and transcription with the tuning done for you, use Dictation (below), built on top of it.

## CUDA acceleration

Compile with `-Dggml_cuda` (Linux only) to offload to NVIDIA GPUs:

```sh
oriel build -Dllama -Dwhisper -Dggml_cuda -Dcuda_path=/opt/cuda
```

Measured speedup on RTX 4070 (11 s audio): 3.2 s on CPU → 0.8 s on CUDA.

Requires the CUDA toolkit and an NVIDIA GPU at runtime; CPU fallback works.

## Phones: ARM CPU kernels (`-Dggml_arm`)

ggml, llama.cpp and whisper.cpp are compiled optimized in every build mode, and for ARM phones with the instructions their fast kernels need: `-Dggml_arm=dotprod` (the Android default: every phone since 2018) or `i8mm` (Armv8.6/v9: Tensor G3+, Snapdragon 8 Gen 1+, Dimensity 9000+). A CPU without them is refused at model load (`error.CpuUnsupported`), not crashed. Mobile GPU drivers often lose to these kernels, per model: on a Pixel's Mali-G715, whisper base ran 1.8× faster on the CPU, small 1.6× faster on Vulkan.

## Metal acceleration (macOS, iOS)

On macOS and iOS, ggml's Metal backend is built in by default (`-Dggml_metal=false` turns it off); the kernel sources are embedded, so no Xcode `metal` compiler is needed. Measured on an Apple M1 (5.9 s clip, tiny.en, incl. model load): 7.3 s on CPU → about 1 s on Metal.

# Audio capture

Record microphones and system audio as mono `f32` samples (16 kHz for whisper).

```zig
const sources = try oriel.audio_capture.listSources(gpa); // .name, .description, .monitor (system audio)
defer oriel.audio_capture.freeSources(gpa, sources);

var stream = try oriel.audio_capture.Stream.open(sources[0].name, "My App", 16000);
defer stream.close();
var buf: [1600]f32 = undefined; // 100 ms
try stream.read(&buf); // blocks until full
```

**Platform support:** Linux (PulseAudio / PipeWire; system audio through monitor sources) · Windows (WASAPI; system audio through loopback of each output) · macOS (CoreAudio; "System audio (all apps)" through a Core Audio process tap on macOS 14.2+, no driver; needs the Microphone or System Audio Recording permission) · Android (AAudio, microphones; a foreground service keeps it going in the background) · iOS (AVAudioSession + AudioQueue, microphones; background audio with `.ios = .{ .background_audio = true }`).

**Status:** Opt-in with `-Daudio_capture`. Default: off.

# Dictation

Voice to text with the tuning built in: live dictation from the microphone (or system audio, for captions), and transcription of recordings. Needs `-Dwhisper -Daudio_capture`.

```zig
oriel.dictation.init(init.io, init.gpa, models_dir);          // once, at startup
const s = try oriel.dictation.start(.{ .language = "de" });    // from an async command
// the page gets dictation:partial, dictation:final and dictation:level events
const r = try oriel.dictation.stop(gpa);                       // r.text: everything said
const t = try oriel.dictation.transcribeFile(gpa, "talk.wav", .{});
```

**Engines** (`.engine`):

- `.whisper`: whisper.cpp on every platform, about 99 languages, offline.
- `.system`: the platform's recognizer, with no model to download. On Android, `SpeechRecognizer`: Google's on-device model on a Pixel, streaming about one update a second. Its languages are the phone's (Oriel asks Android to download a missing language pack).
- `.auto`: the system engine on Android when it runs on the device, otherwise whisper.

**What whisper gets without tuning:**

- Models: tiny, base and small in q8_0, with `download`, `delete` and `status`.
- Silence skipping: Silero voice detection, so silence never reaches whisper.
- Speed: whisper's window sized to the clip.
- Live text from a smaller *draft* model (base under small), while the chosen model writes each phrase when you pause. Each runs on its own faster processor.
- The CPU or the GPU per device and model (`.backend = .auto`): what `compare()` measured, remembered next to the models. Until then, the GPU on desktops and the CPU on phones; on phones the GPU must be 1.3× faster to be picked.

**Files and samples:** `transcribeFile` reads WAV (PCM or float, any rate and channel count). `transcribeSamples` takes 16 kHz mono samples from any decoder.

**Events:** `dictation:level`, `dictation:partial` (the phrase so far, `""` once final), `dictation:final`, `dictation:download`, `dictation:compare`, `dictation:error`, `dictation:ended`. `oriel.dictation.Events` has their types, for the app's own `Events` struct.

**Building blocks:** `oriel.whisper`, `oriel.audio_capture` and `oriel.ggml_gpu` stay public for pipelines of your own.

The showcase's Dictate tab uses all of it, and its System tab dictates into other apps.

# Chat

Chat and completion with a local LLM, the llama.cpp counterpart of Dictation. Needs `-Dllama`.

```zig
oriel.chat.init(init.io, init.gpa, models_dir);              // once, at startup
const r = try oriel.chat.generate(gpa, &.{
    .{ .role = "system", .content = "Answer briefly." },
    .{ .role = "user", .content = "What is Zig?" },
}, .{});                                                      // from an async command
// chat:token events stream the reply; oriel.chat.cancel() stops it
```

**What you get without tuning:**

- Models: small multilingual instruct models in q4_0 (Qwen2.5 0.5B and 1.5B, Llama 3.2 1B), and on desktops Qwen3.5 9B and Gemma 4 12B (a computer with 16 GB of memory runs them), with `download`, `delete` and `status`.
- The model's own chat template (read from its GGUF): `messages` are plain `{ role, content }`. Qwen3.5 and Gemma 4 answer straight away; `.think = true` lets them reason first, and the reasoning stays out of the reply.
- Tuned like llama-server: a resident threadpool, 2048-token prompt batches on desktops, a q8_0 KV cache with flash attention (f16 where the backend has none), the context capped at what the model was trained for and halved when memory runs out, and the CPU when the model doesn't fit on the GPU.
- Structured output: `.schema` takes a JSON schema, and the reply follows it.
- Streaming: `chat:token` events carry whole UTF-8 characters.
- Speed across turns: the conversation's KV cache is reused, so a turn only evaluates what's new.
- Long chats: a conversation longer than the context drops its oldest turns, and the system prompt stays.
- The CPU or the GPU per device and model (`.backend = .auto`), as `compare()` measured it (tokens per second), with a warm-up for GPU models.

**Result:** the text, the stop reason (`eos`, `length`, `cancelled`), the prompt and reply token counts, the tokens reused from the cache, and the tokens per second.

**Building blocks:** `oriel.llama` (the C API and JSON-schema grammars) and `oriel.ggml_gpu`.
